Jersey, Delaware, Pennsylvania, or New York. Note on STEM-OPT Employment Please note that STEM OPT employment is not permitted at Rowan University. To be eligible for a STEM OPT extension, the student's employer must be registered in E-Verify and must use the system to verify all new employees. While Rowan University is registered in the E-Verify system, the University does not use the system to verify all new employees, only those that are working on a Federal Contract. This means that Rowan does not permit individuals to work at the University using a STEM OPT Employment Authorization Document as proof of US Work Authorization. Non-Discrimation at Rowan University Rowan University is committed to creating a welcoming environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ethnicity, race, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, national origin, (dis)ability status, military status, and other NJ protected classes. Rowan University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment as required by Title IX. Rowan is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with (dis)abilities. To request reasonable accommodation, contact Christy Mroz, Administrative Assistant, OEE@rowan.edu, 856-256-5494. Rowan strongly encourages applicants from underrepresented groups to apply. Pursuant to Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 and supporting regulations, Rowan does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education programs or activities that it operates; this extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its supporting regulations may be directed to the Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights, Office for Civil Rights, U.S. Department of Education, or to the University’s Title IX Coordinator, Office of Student Equity & Compliance, Rowan University, Hawthorne Hall, Suite 312, 201 Mullica Hill Rd, Glassboro, NJ 08028, titleIXcoordinator@rowan.edu , 856-256-5440. For information on the Title IX Sexual Harassment/Sexual Assault policy and grievance procedures, please click here . Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Rowan is committed in assisting all members of our University community in providing for their safety and security. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available on the Rowan University Police Department (RUPD), Clery Act webpage here . The report contains information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as crime prevention, RUPD authority/jurisdiction, crime reporting policies, fire safety, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security on all our campuses. The report also contains information about fire statistics in Rowan University on-campus student housing facilities and crime statistics for the three previous calendar years, including reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. This information is required by federal law, Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act or the \"Clery Act\" and is provided by the Rowan University Police Department. If you would like to receive a hard copy of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report which contains this information, you can stop by the RUPD Office, located at Bole Hall Annex, 201 Mullica Hill Road, Glassboro, NJ 08028 or you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (856) 256-4562 or email: cleryact@rowan.edu . Sign In Position Search e.g. \"IRT\", \"Stratford\", \"Glassboro\" Filter Results Work type Regular Full-Time 1 Locations Glassboro, New Jersey 1 Categories School of Veterinary Medicine 1 Rowan on Twitter Rowan on Facebook Rowan on Instagram Rowan on YouTube Rowan on Flickr Rowan University • 201 Mullica Hill Road • Glassboro, New Jersey 08028 • 856-256-4000 ©2025 Rowan University. Consumer Disclosures . Read the Notice of Availability of Rowan’s Annual Security & Fire Safety Report"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/listing/?page=2&page-items=20": {
      "title": "Job Postings",
      "description": "Rowan HR - Recent Jobs Job Postings | Human Resources | Rowan University Skip to main content News Alumni Parents Donors Jobs Apply my Rowan Rowan University Menu Admissions & Aid Show submenu for \"Admissions & Aid\" First-Year Admissions Transfer Admissions Financial Aid Graduate Admissions Medical Education Admissions International Admissions Tours & Open Houses Rowan Online Degree Completion Academics Show submenu for \"Academics\" Colleges & Schools Degrees & Programs Courses, Schedules & Registration Student Success International Winter & Summer Sessions Camden Campus Rowan University Libraries Bookstore Campus Life Show submenu for \"Campus Life\" The Arts at Rowan Athletics & Sports Recreation Health & Safety Housing & Dining Technology on Campus Entertainment & Culture Center for Well-being Health & Medicine Show submenu for \"Health & Medicine\" Cooper Medical School of Rowan University (MD) Virtua Health College of Medicine & Life Sciences (DO) Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) Research Show submenu for \"Research\" Office of Research Research Centers & Institutes South Jersey Technology Park Research News Military/Veterans Thrive About Show submenu for \"About\" Leadership Our Past, Present & Future Visiting Rowan Working at Rowan Rowan Fast Facts Giving to Rowan News & Events Contact Us Search Search Rowan Search People Search Job Postings Rowan University » Human Resources » Job Postings Job Postings Welcome to Rowan University’s Career Site A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to nearly 25,000 students. The fastest-growing public research institution in the Northeast and among the country’s top 10 fastest-growing, Rowan offers a thriving multidisciplinary environment with a strong emphasis on practical research in health care, engineering, science and business, while ensuring excellence in undergraduate education. Nationally recognized for innovation, high-quality, affordable education and public-private partnerships, Rowan is one of two universities in the U.S. to offer M.D., D.O. and D.V.M. degree programs. For more information on Rowan University, click here . All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Rowan Employee Benefits Rowan University offers a comprehensive benefits package to its staff and faculty members* including health, prescription, and dental coverage, vision reimbursement, a variety of investment options including mandatory pension programs and voluntary retirement savings opportunities, tuition benefits and scholarships, and paid time off. For more information on available benefits at Rowan, please visit the Benefits website . Benefits available to employees of the Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine can be viewed here . *Available benefits are dependent upon employee class and union affiliation. Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Instructional Designer (PSS2), Rowan Online Glassboro, New Jersey Oct 1 2026 Join Rowan Online as an Instructional Designer and help shape high-impact, engaging online learning experiences in a fast-growing digital education environment. This hybrid role in Glassboro, NJ offers a competitive salary ($76K–$87K), flexible work arrangements, and the opportunity to collaborate with faculty while leveraging cutting-edge instructional technology and LMS platforms like Canvas. Make a measurable impact on student success while advancing your career with strong benefits, tuition reimbursement, and a mission-driven team focused on innovation in online education. Account Manager Workforce Learning Solutions, Healthcare Vertical Glassboro, New Jersey Oct 1 2026 Take the lead in transforming healthcare education as Rowan Online’s Account Manager for Workforce Learning Solutions – Healthcare, where your strategic partnerships drive enrollment growth, student success, and workforce readiness. With competitive salary and full NJ State benefits including tuition reimbursement for you and your family this role puts you at the center of building and sustaining long-term relationships with hospitals, healthcare organizations, and professional associations. Join a collaborative, impact-driven team in downtown Glassboro, NJ, and shape workforce learning initiatives that empower students, support partners, and elevate Rowan Online’s healthcare programs. Temporary Part Time Hourly Grant Administrator (Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences) Glassboro, New Jersey Jan 27 2027 Reporting to the Dean of the Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences, the Grant Administrator is a part-time position needed to support faculty members in the college with developing proposals and to assist in the expansion of a successful grant portfolio program. This includes coordinating with the University’s Research Office, supporting the writing, budget, and submission process, researching and identifying potential grant opportunities, training faculty members on grant writing, managing the submission and reporting calendar, and meeting all deadlines as required. Adjunct Professor - School of Innovation and Entrepreneurship Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Adjunct Professors of Innovation and Entrepreneurship sought for Rohrer College of Business, School of Innovation and Entrepreneurship. Adjunct Faculty - Department of Communication Studies Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 The Communication Studies Department at Rowan University is seeking adjuncts to teach Public Speaking and Digital Presentations. The ability to teach additional courses such as Interpersonal Communication, Business & Professional Communication, and Technical Speaking for Engineers is a plus. Experience in teaching online and working with Neurodivergent and Honors students is also a desired asset. Qualified candidates must have at least an MA or MS in Communication Studies (or a closely related field) as well as teaching experience at the college level. Having the flexibility to teach various times during the day, especially 8 AM is preferred. Adjunct Faculty - Department of History Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 The Department of History seeks to create a pool of adjunct faculty qualified to teach survey-level courses in Western Civilization, World History, and United States History. Clinical Instructor, Respiratory Therapy Program Sewell, New Jersey Rowan University is accepting applications for the position of Clinical Instructor in the Respiratory Therapy Program. Offering entry-level and degree-advancement programs leading to the Bachelor of Science in Respiratory Therapy, the Rowan University Respiratory Therapy program is located in the new Health Sciences Center on the campus of Rowan College of Jersey in Sewell, NJ.  The entry-level and degree-advancement baccalaureate programs hold provisional accreditation by the Council on Accreditation for Respiratory Care (CoARC). Adjunct Professor, Marketing, Management Information Systems, and Supply Chain - Department of Marketing and Business Information Systems Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Adjunct Professors of Marketing, Management Information Systems, and Supply Chain sought for Rohrer College of Business, Marketing and Business Information Systems Department. Veterinary Ophthalmologist (Full-Time or Part-Time Faculty, Open Rank) - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Glassboro, New Jersey Oct 30 2026 The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine (SSVM) at Rowan University is seeking an experienced Veterinary Ophthalmologist to join our growing Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital. Full-time and part-time appointments will be considered, offering flexibility for candidates seeking a clinical, academic, or blended professional role.\nThis is an exciting opportunity to join an established and thriving Ophthalmology Service within one of the nation's newest veterinary schools. The successful candidate will become part of an active specialty practice with a growing clinical caseload while contributing to the continued development of SSVM's clinical education mission.\nAs a member of the Ophthalmology Service, you will provide advanced patient care, collaborate with a multidisciplinary team of specialists, and play an important role in educating future veterinarians while helping shape the culture and educational approach of a new veterinary program.\nWhether you are an experienced academic ophthalmologist, a private specialty practitioner seeking a collaborative academic environment, or a clinician interested in a flexible faculty appointment, SSVM offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on patients, students, and the veterinary profession. Adjunct Faculty - Department of Health and Exercise Science Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Adjunct Faculty Position in the Department of Health and Exercise Science. Adjunct Faculty, Department of Geography, Planning, & Sustainability Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 The Department of Geography, Planning, and Sustainability is seeking dedicated adjunct instructors in topics served by our degree programs. Adjunct Faculty – EdS in School Psychology Instructor/Internship Supervisor, Department of Wellness and Inclusive Services in Education Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 The College of Education is searching for a qualified and experienced school psychologist to supervise field experiences and/or teach professional courses within the EdS in School Psychology program. The successful candidate is expected to be familiar with the National Association of School Psychologists (NASP) professional standards including the comprehensive NASP practice model This is a part-time, adjunct position with the possibility of renewal. Emergency and Critical Care Section Head - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Glassboro, New Jersey Oct 30 2026 The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University (SSVM) is seeking a Small Animal Medicine Section Head to join our new veterinary program and teaching hospital.  The hospital is located 1.5 miles from our main Glassboro campus. Adjunct Faculty - Department of Art Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 The Department of Art at Rowan University is seeking qualified adjuncts to teach undergraduate courses in Studio Art, Drawing, Painting, 2 and 3-d Design, Graphic Design and Digital Media, Ceramics, Sculpture, Jewelry/Metals, and Art History. Courses will be taught on the main campus in Glassboro, New Jersey Adjunct Faculty – Construction Management, Henry M. Rowan College of Engineering Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Adjunct Faculty – Construction Management, Henry M. Rowan College of Engineering Adjunct Faculty (Online) - Department of Psychology Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Rowan University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions leading online course offerings. The majority of our online courses in Psychology serve our undergraduate population. If you are interested in and available for teaching in person, please see our ad recruiting for in person instructors for additional application details. Adjunct Faculty (In-person and Online), BS in Healthcare Management and Administration and MS in Healthcare Management (HCM) Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 In-person and Online Adjunct Faculty\nFor Programs: BS in Healthcare Management and Administration and MS in Healthcare Management (HCM) Positions Adjunct Faculty - Special Education Instructors - Supervisors of Field Experiences Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 The College of Education is searching for qualified and experienced special education/inclusive education specialists to supervise field experiences and/or teach in person or online classes at the undergraduate and graduate level. The successful candidate will demonstrate familiarity with the accreditation standards of national associations in special education, such as the Council for Exceptional Children.  This is a part-time, adjunct position with the possibility of renewal. The position requires availability during the regular school day. Per Diem Psychiatrist, Department of Psychiatry, Rowan-Virtua SOM Mount Laurel, New Jersey Sep 18 2026 Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine is currently seeking a psychiatrist to join our growing Department of Psychiatry located in Southern New Jersey. This is a per-diem position within the Department of Psychiatry. The selected candidate will be expected to provide appropriate, comprehensive, and multidisciplinary care. Responsibilities include inpatient and outpatient psychiatric services within multiple health systems in South Jersey. This role will work closely with the clinical staff for the day-to-day treatment of patients as well as in an academic capacity to teach medical students, residents, and allied health professionals. This position is available for academic promotion within the university. Adjunct Faculty, Philosophy - Department of Philosophy and World Religions Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 The Department of Philosophy and World Religions seeks qualified adjunct faculty for various philosophy classes, including: Logic of Everyday Reasoning (informal logic), Philosophical Perspectives on Science (a gen-ed philosophy of science course for non-majors), Intro to Philosophy, Intro to Ethics, Social & Political Philosophy, and Intro to Symbolic Logic. More Jobs 89 Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Instructional Designer (PSS2), Rowan Online Glassboro, New Jersey Oct 1 2026 Account Manager Workforce Learning Solutions, Healthcare Vertical Glassboro, New Jersey Oct 1 2026 Temporary Part Time Hourly Grant Administrator (Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences) Glassboro, New Jersey Jan 27 2027 Adjunct Professor - School of Innovation and Entrepreneurship Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Adjunct Faculty - Department of Communication Studies Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Adjunct Faculty - Department of History Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Clinical Instructor, Respiratory Therapy Program Sewell, New Jersey Adjunct Professor, Marketing, Management Information Systems, and Supply Chain - Department of Marketing and Business Information Systems Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Veterinary Ophthalmologist (Full-Time or Part-Time Faculty, Open Rank) - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Glassboro, New Jersey Oct 30 2026 Adjunct Faculty - Department of Health and Exercise Science Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Adjunct Faculty, Department of Geography, Planning, & Sustainability Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Adjunct Faculty – EdS in School Psychology Instructor/Internship Supervisor, Department of Wellness and Inclusive Services in Education Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Emergency and Critical Care Section Head - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Glassboro, New Jersey Oct 30 2026 Adjunct Faculty - Department of Art Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Adjunct Faculty – Construction Management, Henry M. Rowan College of Engineering Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Adjunct Faculty (Online) - Department of Psychology Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Adjunct Faculty (In-person and Online), BS in Healthcare Management and Administration and MS in Healthcare Management (HCM) Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Adjunct Faculty - Special Education Instructors - Supervisors of Field Experiences Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 Per Diem Psychiatrist, Department of Psychiatry, Rowan-Virtua SOM Mount Laurel, New Jersey Sep 18 2026 Adjunct Faculty, Philosophy - Department of Philosophy and World Religions Glassboro, New Jersey Jun 30 2027 More Jobs 89 Powered by PageUp More Information Residency Requirements Rowan University is subject to the residency requirements of the NJ First Act (N.J.S.A. 52:14-7, P.L. 2011, Chapter 70). Any person hired to a non-exempt position shall either have their principal residence in New Jersey or have one (1) year from the date of employment to establish, and then maintain, principal residence in the State of New Jersey. Any person hired to an exempt position shall either have their principal residence in New Jersey, Delaware, Pennsylvania, or New York or have ninety (90) days from the date of employment to establish, then maintain, principal residence in the State of New Jersey, Delaware, Pennsylvania, or New York. Note on STEM-OPT Employment Please note that STEM OPT employment is not permitted at Rowan University. To be eligible for a STEM OPT extension, the student's employer must be registered in E-Verify and must use the system to verify all new employees. While Rowan University is registered in the E-Verify system, the University does not use the system to verify all new employees, only those that are working on a Federal Contract. This means that Rowan does not permit individuals to work at the University using a STEM OPT Employment Authorization Document as proof of US Work Authorization. Non-Discrimation at Rowan University Rowan University is committed to creating a welcoming environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ethnicity, race, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, national origin, (dis)ability status, military status, and other NJ protected classes. Rowan University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment as required by Title IX. Rowan is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with (dis)abilities. To request reasonable accommodation, contact Christy Mroz, Administrative Assistant, OEE@rowan.edu, 856-256-5494. Rowan strongly encourages applicants from underrepresented groups to apply. Pursuant to Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 and supporting regulations, Rowan does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education programs or activities that it operates; this extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about the application of Title IX and its supporting regulations may be directed to the Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights, Office for Civil Rights, U.S. Department of Education, or to the University’s Title IX Coordinator, Office of Student Equity & Compliance, Rowan University, Hawthorne Hall, Suite 312, 201 Mullica Hill Rd, Glassboro, NJ 08028, titleIXcoordinator@rowan.edu , 856-256-5440. For information on the Title IX Sexual Harassment/Sexual Assault policy and grievance procedures, please click here . Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Rowan is committed in assisting all members of our University community in providing for their safety and security. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available on the Rowan University Police Department (RUPD), Clery Act webpage here . The report contains information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as crime prevention, RUPD authority/jurisdiction, crime reporting policies, fire safety, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security on all our campuses. The report also contains information about fire statistics in Rowan University on-campus student housing facilities and crime statistics for the three previous calendar years, including reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. This information is required by federal law, Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act or the \"Clery Act\" and is provided by the Rowan University Police Department. If you would like to receive a hard copy of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report which contains this information, you can stop by the RUPD Office, located at Bole Hall Annex, 201 Mullica Hill Road, Glassboro, NJ 08028 or you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (856) 256-4562 or email: cleryact@rowan.edu . Sign In Position Search e.g. \"IRT\", \"Stratford\", \"Glassboro\" Filter Results Work type Per Diem 6 Regular Full-Time 50 Regular Part-Time 6 Temporary Full-Time 3 Temporary Part-Time 70 Locations Camden, New Jersey 2 Glassboro, New Jersey 101 Mount Laurel, New Jersey 3 Sewell, New Jersey 8 Stratford, New Jersey 16 Categories Administrative - Clerical 5 Clinical 3 Facilities - Maintenance 9 Faculty - College of Business 7 Faculty - College of Education 8 Faculty - College of Graduate and Continuing Education 1 Faculty - College of Science and Mathematics 10 Faculty - College of the Arts 7 Faculty - Cooper Medical School of Rowan University 2 Faculty - Henry M. Rowan College of Engineering 9 Faculty - Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences 24 Faculty - School of Nursing & Health Professions 5 Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine 20 Faculty - University College/School of Professional Studies 3 Managerial 1 Professional 10 Public Safety/Security 3 School of Veterinary Medicine 21 Rowan on Twitter Rowan on Facebook Rowan on Instagram Rowan on YouTube Rowan on Flickr Rowan University • 201 Mullica Hill Road • Glassboro, New Jersey 08028 • 856-256-4000 ©2025 Rowan University. Consumer Disclosures . Read the Notice of Availability of Rowan’s Annual Security & Fire Safety Report"
